any problems when it comes to the logistics aspect of it. We'll be doing signage at the previous location both electronic signs but physical signs. We are speaking with the Council on Aging potentially on having the van available for transportation for residents who don't have transportation in that area but are already at that location.

66
00:30:12,288 --> 00:30:39,305
Additional signage will be placed at Tufts Scanter Center as well, directing people to the back of the building where the entrance is, which is the handicap accessible entrance. Additionally, we'll have parking there available in that lot just adjacent to that entrance as well. All right. Great. Do we have any questions regarding this? And this is temporary due to the construction at Walkland Court. Yeah. Unfortunately, the construction will take

67
00:30:39,777 --> 00:31:02,862
a year, potentially more, so it could be this cycle and the next. So 2028 is the hope, but unfortunately I can't predict that. All right. And so we will go to Councilor Scarpelli. I think that this has happened before, and the team has done a great job, but I think

68
00:31:03,706 --> 00:31:28,462
just to reassure everybody, there'll be a communication plan in place that would really educate everybody in enough time. I know that we have, what, a primary in a couple of weeks, so is there, are there plans in place to make sure that? So as long as you guys approve this this evening, tomorrow morning, the mail will be dropped. Okay. That will be going out to every resident of, every voter rather, of Ward 4, Precinct 2.

69
00:31:28,462 --> 00:31:57,976
with a postcard saying, hey, this is where the new location is going to be, as well as an option of vote-by-mail for those who aren't able to get to the new polling location for whatever reason. They can scan the QR code. They can get onto the website, submit a vote-by-mail application that would go to me directly, and then we would produce the vote-by-mail to them. So they have several weeks to get that done. But additionally, the mayor's office and I discussed using the reverse 911 system

70
00:31:58,162 --> 00:32:20,977
to be able to contact all the voters in that specific district. We'll be doing postings on the website as well as informational going out in the mayor's kind of newsletter. Thank you. That's perfect. All right. Any further questions, members of the council on the relocation? Seeing none, is there a motion?

71
