qualify for time served. And part of that is that's why the Voya system is in there as well. So you could pull from that instead of having, you don't pay into a pension.

78
00:35:13,962 --> 00:35:42,430
being an employee or an auction worker, you pay into the VOIA because it's a part-time position for all intents and purposes. OK. Has this impacted getting poll workers this year? Yes, it has. All right. And when you say other cities are using this, are a lot of cities using this? Yes. Most are. I would say a large majority are. All right. This is one of the changing times things. I mean, we used to be able to just do something the way we always did it.

79
00:35:43,342 --> 00:36:11,455
It's impacted it in the sense of potentially we could lose very good people who volunteered for the city for a long time, but we're working to make sure that we don't lose any steps when it comes to having people work at the locations. We've already posted something online under human resources for anyone who is interested at home, who's listening. If you'd like to be a poll worker, please fill out an application. I'll be happy to get back to you. We can get you in trained and we can get things worked for that way.

80
00:36:12,147 --> 00:36:41,003
And how are we looking recruitment-wise? I would say about 85% right now, but I'm not concerned at all about having to be fully staffed by September 1st. All right. Great. Thank you. Any further questions, members of the Council? Seeing none, on the motion, Mr. Clerk, please call the roll. Councilor Kelly? Councilor Lemming? Yes. Councilor Maloney?

