01:00:17,002 --> 01:00:41,082
Thank you. Seeing no further comments from city councillors, I will go to public comment. If you would like to make a comment in the room, you can come line up at the podium or raise your hand on Zoom. Everybody can have three minutes to speak and you can state your name and location for the record. One moment.

141
01:00:50,431 --> 01:00:58,497
Go ahead. Hello, I'm Genesis Perez. You said address as well? Your location.

142
01:00:59,189 --> 01:01:29,176
Yeah, so 229 Main Street. So yeah, hello everyone. My name is Genesis. I'm a Tufts graduate student and worker as well as a Medford resident. Like many people here, I'm relatively new to the city. I've only been here like four years. But Medford has welcomed me and many other students like me who are just trying to make the most of our studies. Unfortunately, Tufts University has been less welcoming of late.

143
01:01:29,176 --> 01:01:49,392
Tufts is trying to unfairly dismiss one of our international union siblings from our PhD program in retaliation for reporting wage theft. International grad workers' legal status in this country is contingent upon their student status, which means that the student will be forced to leave the country and this wonderful city that we call home.

144
01:01:49,392 --> 01:02:05,693
Tufts is weaponizing the precarity of international workers and the culture of fear that is being fomented by this current federal administration to force international grad workers to accept unfair and unsafe labor conditions and that we find unacceptable.

145
01:02:05,693 --> 01:02:22,906
We did speak a little bit about this earlier, but to summarize again, this grad worker was given additional TA or a teaching assistant work on top of her normal RA, research assistant workload. She was not paid for this additional work, violating our contract.

146
01:02:22,906 --> 01:02:39,308
After struggling to keep up due to this additional labor, her advisor told her that her performance was inadequate and that her summer appointment had been canceled, despite her 12-month contract. He instead proposed an alternative summer workload, which would oust her from the union.

147
01:02:39,308 --> 01:03:03,254
After this grad worker reached out to the union about this concerning proposal, Dean Karen Panetta outed her by name to her entire department via email. In response, her advisor retroactively changed her fall and spring grades for her RA appointment to unsatisfactory grades in violation of Tufts' own grading policies.

148
01:03:04,638 --> 01:03:15,252
Dean Panetta is now attempting to use these grades that were retroactively assigned as an excuse to dismiss the student from her PhD program, ending her student visa as well.

149
01:03:16,484 --> 01:03:35,468
We have supported our union sibling through the formal grievance process, but Tufts has denied any accountability and has issued contradictory statements. They have been consistently late to respond to our arguments, even missing yesterday's deadline for step two of the grievance progress, despite their claims that they are

150
01:03:35,468 --> 01:03:57,355
attempting to be reasonable, we can see that we can only assume that they are counting on all of this to go away once the student's visa status expires later this month and they're trying to run out the clock. Tufts actions show that they do not actually care about international students at all and that they are willing to do anything to get away with exploiting grad workers.

151
01:03:57,355 --> 01:04:14,669
Our demands of Tufts are as follows, reinstate the grad workers summer RA funding, reinstate the grad workers position in the PhD program, provide retroactive payment to all grad workers who have been forced to do unpaid TA work, and provide the grad worker with transitional support to a new lab.

152
01:04:15,530 --> 01:04:41,112
We believe these are reasonable demands, and we have been surprised by Tufts' obstinate refusal to meet them. The mechanism Tufts is using to dismiss the grad worker, retroactively changing grades, is arbitrary and violates all of the university's academic standards. If Tufts gets away with this unjust dismissal, they will see no reason to uphold their part of the contract when international workers are involved, leaving them particularly vulnerable to abuse and witch theft.

153
01:04:41,112 --> 01:04:59,523
Additionally, Tufts has allowed dangerous work conditions in the past which have only improved due to our union's vigilance and strict enforcement of our contract. Any contract violations leave all Tufts workers at risk of further exploitation and put all of us in more danger. You are one minute over right now. Sorry.

154
01:04:59,523 --> 01:05:25,696
The Tufts community is a major part of Medford. Exploitation of workers anywhere lowers not only their standard of living, but also their disposable income, which could be invested into local businesses. But most importantly, international students should not feel unsafe in our city after witnessing ICE's unjust and terrifying abduction of Rumesa Ozturk last year. How can we stand aside and watch as Tufts robs another international student?

155
01:05:25,696 --> 01:05:48,595
and Medford community member of the chance to pursue her studies with security and dignity. Please stand in solidarity with us. Thank you very much. Thank you. Seeing no hands on zoom, I will go back to the podium. Please state your name for the record.

156
01:05:49,405 --> 01:06:07,563
Yes, Simon Alcindor, 44 Tainter Street. And I just wanted to say that I really do thank the council for taking this up because as somebody who is currently an undergraduate student who is looking to get into organizing, not even necessarily with the union, like things like this are freaking terrifying.

157
01:06:07,563 --> 01:06:36,436
The fact that at any university we've seen over the past few years, they are willing to just basically strip away any rights you think that you may have while on a campus in order to go after people who dare speak out against the shitty things that universities do constantly. I think that is something that we need to continue pressing on because when it goes unchecked, as we are seeing across many universities in Boston, universities will basically just do whatever they want.

158
01:06:36,655 --> 01:06:57,395
whether it's not really protecting international students when it comes to ICE, whether it comes to punishing students for speaking out about Palestine. These universities will really do whatever they want when they are not checked with the power that they have. So, again, I just really want to commend the Council for taking up this matter and really want to push you all to keep on doing this in the future.

159
01:06:57,395 --> 01:07:23,500
And especially keep your ears to the ground when it comes to things that are not inside a union, because there are a lot of students who are really threatened by this type of stuff who don't have the support of a union, especially undergraduate students almost certainly don't in most cases. So, yeah, thank you. Thank you. Please state your name for the record. Go ahead. Micah Kesselman, 499 Main Street.

160
01:07:23,956 --> 01:07:51,226
I just wanted to say, I'm not affiliated with Tufts. I'm not a student. I'm not a labor advocate or activist. I am just a resident in South Medford, which is one of the neighborhoods that hosts, that actually hosts Tufts campus. And I just want everyone at Tufts to know, especially the impacted students and union members,

161
01:07:52,188 --> 01:08:17,483
that the neighborhood is in support of them. I don't know anyone in my neighborhood worth a damn who doesn't find everything about Tufts conduct here both abhorrent and absolutely enraging. So this is not how our neighborhood treats our neighbors or our guests. And it sure as hell isn't how Tufts should be doing it either. So that's it. Thank you.

162
01:08:23,491 --> 01:08:50,727
