The next paper is 26-137, Resolution to Support Tufts Facilities Workers' Bargaining for a Fair Contract, offered by President Bares. Whereas the City of Medford and its residents share a strong interest in seeing through a good quality union contract between Tufts and its facilities workers who belong to SEIU,

165
01:09:27,937 --> 01:09:51,865
32BJ, and whereas these essential workers are employed as utility workers, as maintenance mechanics in the grounds department and in a variety of trades positions, such as carpenters, locksmiths, HVAC mechanics, plumbers, electricians, and more, and whereas as the largest private employer in Medford and Somerville and a major Boston area employer, Tufts University has a vitally important role

166
01:09:51,865 --> 01:10:12,368
and setting standards for all working people, particularly those to whom the university owes its buildings, condition functioning, and its outstanding grounds. And whereas these proud 32 BJSCIU members' demands for a fair contract are reasonable, fair family-sustaining wage increases, lower health care monthly

167
01:10:12,368 --> 01:10:35,825
lower monthly health care premiums, trying to get me, protections for immigrant workers, union benefits and other richly deserved improvements. Now, therefore, be it resolved by the Medford City Council that we call on Tufts University to support the contract demands of Tufts facilities workers and just an example of fair treatment and good labor relations for other area employers. President Behrs.

168
01:10:38,693 --> 01:10:55,940
Thank you, Vice President Lazaro. Similarly to what I was saying in the last resolution, Tufts needs to be a good neighbor. It needs to treat its workers fairly. It needs to treat the city of Medford fairly. It needs to treat its students fairly.

169
01:10:56,480 --> 01:11:14,502
The facilities workers at Tufts who are members of 32BJSCIU deserve a fair contract. They are in a contract campaign right now. They are fighting for I think completely reasonable conditions in their contract.

170
01:11:14,502 --> 01:11:40,979
around affordability, about fair wages, about addressing the cost of healthcare, about protecting immigrant workers, just like we were just hearing about the international graduate workers. And this is something that also the city council takes very seriously when it comes to the city of Medford and making sure that we're not part of the problem when it comes to a race to the bottom or not treating workers fairly.

171
01:11:42,059 --> 01:11:53,905
And I think that's just something that's really important for Tufts to show as a value to represent here in our city. And at the end of the day, right?

